        form: '<table><tr><th>Element</th><th>Question to ask</th></tr><tr><td>Claim</td><td>What exactly is the writer saying?</td></tr><tr><td>Evidence</td><td>What supports it? Data, examples, experts, anecdotes? How strong is it?</td></tr><tr><td>Assumption</td><td>What must be true for the argument to work, but isn\'t stated?</td></tr><tr><td>Bias / interest</td><td>Who is writing, and what might they gain?</td></tr><tr><td>Counterarguments</td><td>Are other views considered fairly?</td></tr></table><table><tr><th>Common fallacies</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>Hasty generalization</td><td>“Everyone knows students can\'t concentrate.”</td></tr><tr><td>Anecdotal evidence</td><td>“We struggled and turned out fine.”</td></tr><tr><td>Ad hominem</td><td>“They would say that — they want to sell.”</td></tr><tr><td>False dilemma</td><td>“Either we ban it, or…”</td></tr><tr><td>Slippery slope</td><td>“If we allow X, soon Y and Z will happen.”</td></tr><tr><td>Correlation ≠ causation</td><td>“Since AI appeared, grades fell, so AI caused it.”</td></tr></table>',
